# The Moments switch's kernel floor: the privacy switch driver learns once per
# boot which sensors the switch blocks (a mask: 1 microphone, 2 camera) and
# refuses every later write. Until this write it blocks everything while the
# switch is down. system_server keeps the property equal to the owner's
# Moments action; a change takes effect at the next boot.
#
# After init.rc's post-fs-data, which loads the persistent properties and
# waits for them, and before the audio and camera services start.
on post-fs-data
    write /sys/kernel/privacy_switch/policy ${persist.diamaneos.privacy_switch.policy:-0}
